   draft's notice leads the page instead of waiting below the fold, and where the floating fullscreen toggle
   exists the whole frame keeps clear of its corner, not just the brand row.
   ponytail: 1.8.14 was written straight into this pre-built bundle (as 1.8.13 was): this block, the
   coarse-pointer 16px field floor in the shell sheet, and obScroll() with its calls in re() and qe().
   The source of truth is the package's own source tree outside this repository; until the change is
   mirrored there, tests/gacha-forge-location-ids.regression.mjs fails any bundle drop that loses it. */
@media (orientation: landscape) and (max-height: 500px) {
  .gf-stage:has(.ob-root) { width: 100%; }
  .ob-frame { display: block; padding: .35rem .75rem 0; overflow-y: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain; }
  .ob-intake { width: 100%; min-height: 100%; max-height: none; gap: .35rem; }
  .ob-step { gap: .35rem; }
  .ob-step .ob-grid { flex: none; overflow: visible; padding-right: 0; }
  .ob-mark { display: none; }
  .ob-steps button { padding-top: .25rem; gap: .3rem; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .ob-steps .n { width: 1.05rem; height: 1.05rem; }
  .ob-error { padding: .3rem .6rem; }
  .ob-error.-note { order: -1; }
  .ob-back, .ob-cancel, .ob-next, .ob-forge { padding-top: .42rem; padding-bottom: .42rem; }
  .ob-presets { padding: .3rem .7rem; }
  .gf-stage:has(> .gf-fs-exit) .ob-frame { padding-right: 2.6rem; }
  .ob-nav { position: sticky; bottom: 0; z-index: 3; margin: auto -.75rem 0; padding: .3rem .75rem .35rem; background: var(--ink); }
